  "narrative": {
    "intro": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligated $14.5B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance won 25 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $581M and obligations up 8.6% year over year. TriWest Healthcare Alliance revenue is concentrated in two agencies. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $9.8B to TriWest Healthcare Alliance, and the Department of Defense obligated $4.7B. TriWest Healthcare Alliance work is concentrated in Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers, which obligated $14.2B, followed by Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds, which obligated $288M. Historical obligations show a steady climb through FY25 and into FY26: FY21 was $6.7B, FY22 was $7.4B, FY23 was $8B, FY24 was $8.4B, FY25 was $13.4B, and FY26 is $14.5B. This profile reflects large, high-dollar awards and a heavy tilt toward health insurance and benefit-management markets within federal buying.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has TriWest Healthcare Alliance's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligated $6.7B in FY21 and climbed each year to $14.5B in FY26 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations rose sharply between FY24 and FY25, from $8.4B to $13.4B, and obligations are up 8.6% year over year into FY26. TriWest Healthcare Alliance average award size in FY26 to date is $581M, reflecting a small number of very large awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are TriWest Healthcare Alliance's biggest customers and what markets do they serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, with $9.8B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the dominant market at $14.2B, with Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $288M. TriWest Healthcare Alliance business is therefore concentrated in veteran and defense healthcare and benefit administration."
      }
    ]
  },
